problems.solution:
先计算分母

$$
(\sqrt{3}+\mathrm{i})^2=2+2\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i}=2\left(1+\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i}\right)
$$

于是

$$
\frac{1-\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i}}{(\sqrt{3}+\mathrm{i})^2}
=\frac{(1-\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i})^2}{2\left(1+\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i}\right)\left(1-\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i}\right)}
=\frac{-2-2\sqrt{3}\mathrm{i}}{8}
=-\frac14-\frac{\sqrt{3}}4\mathrm{i}
$$

故选 B.

